  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14182164/assets/1e151e2518ad2297f86aa25ebdd395ac62c2d05f9e6781d0d82e66a10418aa5a.png)\n\nGiven the diagram shown above, what is the measure of $\\overset{―}{CD}?$",
  "worked_solution": "The segments addition postulate can be applied to a set of more than three collinear points. In the given situation, it states that \n\n$$\nAD=AB+BC+CD.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known values into the equation above, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =AB+BC+CD \\\\ 54 & =17+22+CD \\\\ 54 & =39+CD \\\\ 54-39 & =CD \\\\ CD & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$",
